  "evidence": [
    "Pinned executable dyna_load 4C6BB0 and init 4C69B0 capture provider vtable before Wave::get_attrib, reread device_ afterward, then call captured slot27. This ordering is real; historical decision wave-manual-self-dispatch-20260920 retained it while the external contract was unknown.",
    "Pinned SoundX SHA256 ac272e244b3f1339d9ce63bc2e7acf76605c6ac2695bba3230e72ea59039a3f5: mode1 ctor10035190 calls10028750 clearing provider+3C. Factory post-constructor10001F96->10028B70 updates filename+4C only. Slot28 table10065738+70 ->10001BEA->10035A30 calls10028F40; its only possible nested callback is guarded by the cleared+3C. Remaining operations read fields. Thus the just-created provider getter cannot replace the owner device or its vptr on this pinned path.",
    "Slot27 table10065738+6C ->10002428->100359C0 consumes one dword, returns zero and ret4. Existing SoundDeviceInterface::set_attrib(unsigned long) expresses this contract; caller ignores return. Wave::get_attrib and its relevant Wave subclasses introduce no other override with mutation.",
    "Compute get_attrib first, then issue the typed provider set_attrib call on reread device_. Do not generalize equivalence to arbitrary replacement DLLs or reentrant providers; no bug fixes or method/claim/span changes. Retain load guards, creation errors, attach order and raw flags second setter in init.",
    "Verify whole Wave TU baseline/candidate measurements, actual-body controls including failing mutants, fresh build/link, references and claim continuity. Manual coordinator integration only; no full preservation/game acceptance claim."
  ],
  "intent": "Replace manual newly-created Wave provider attribute dispatch with the evidenced typed contract; preserve original behavior and matching obligations.",
